Initialises the simulation by allocating memory and computing grid dimensions. This function performs critical setup: 1. Calculates internal resolution based on window size and downsampling 2. Resizes canvas to match resolution 3. Computes tile grid dimensions for spatial optimisation 4. Allocates typed arrays for state storage 5. Creates image buffer for rendering
Kind: global function
Emits: window#resize - Automatically called when window is resized (debounced)
Example
